TXe57lUgwPdOn47vFskTBkG6GZ9NGOe_61Lg_RgE1fhBHvB-sQLfpeeF5mpHzO9jgtMH-LkCV9o52wwQFTm8n7YpFu5k1Q_Il6zB_Xtp-8ysiVt7Hm0QJ13pg1vk0uX_nlKD1CGFc_ZhwmL3Ix6SK8nxIDYVigbYHXnsYs_S9vWjp_IXwNk-tP-edZLnjZTajY3UemJ9jEvRmMgspo_Kth-YW47pAdId5UL2vyErkQAQhCEplWlnwbLw7HOa6LcmsS1BF8WrxfFYjxye-fId8w8FwpDL_4o6Pf-lVniPj1CatXDC_H39B2M6H0WfRwXeMgjRF5qcN0krXdIN5_E-zLT3fzrCVDqv8R86xH32W_PWqCZmnL7KBrGvs9EWErvT2RcG7BQkllw1y7mfYyUGvcBwfzyxjeGTPVoeYL3GduIRnwKWMH-tBXWfXqikZfuAejS2-2q6JRPdHFQ1EvYuunQgEIHZYx61NxTvqxiNmkNryMVTcWSzjPmQQSWyQGg6bCFBLzbUu-uUfMuHbAh7LmFYYtD0hXwhf5FBSNWcnEiKWnLtxaKIY9kepx8Knt0D_lYrs-C_l-BN3btR39QYqiNbUmB5zDzsndEmN6JuhsqyLdxujse0Vk9VlibkmnoBSdnrkZyDb6AVM_BTeTkhneENjqI8glpevHatfecvh2Ujpxmi42DJWUwGqlwgLEkvLba2Rx4Y0o0cQx1lt9ClyFLVil5QvspK98gHW17Njcc3A-yayCH2vJCetbQbqo-3QHR_WfZ"},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0c17af8fc60a9be3016adb511a418c8191944eada3cec33375","call_id":"call_3ea90ff727a64ded94c213ba62ab044b","name":"check_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"base_input\":\"prior-candidate.json\",\"reset_base\":true,\"patches\":[{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/propositions/9/source/declaration\",\"value\":\"Real.volume_Icc\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/propositions/9/source/module\",\"value\":\"Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Lebesgue.Basic\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/propositions/-\",\"value\":{\"id\":\"M013\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For an outer measure μ and sets A⊆B, μ(A)≤μ(B).\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[],\"source\":{\"statement\":\"For an outer measure μ and sets A⊆B, μ(A)≤μ(B).\",\"hypotheses\":[\"μ is an outer measure on the ambient type; A and B are sets; A⊆B.\"],\"declaration\":\"MeasureTheory.measure_mono\",\"module\":\"Mathlib.MeasureTheory.OuterMeasure.Basic\"}}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/inputs/-\",\"value\":\"M013\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/applications/-\",\"value\":{\"input\":\"M013\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"bindings\":\"Instantiate μ with Lebesgue volume on ℝ and A=J_i∩[0,1], B=[a_i,b_i], the enclosing closed interval.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"A⊆B by the interval-enclosure construction; volume is a measure and hence an outer measure.\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/uses/-\",\"value\":\"M013\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"value\":\"Assume D>0 and fix 0<s<D; regard s as a positive NNReal exponent d and use the corresponding real coercion in M008. Define C_a(A,δ)=inf{∑'ᵢ ediam(Uᵢ)^a : U:ℕ→Set(X), A⊆⋃ᵢUᵢ, ∀i ediam(Uᵢ)≤δ}. Empty members have ediam 0; for a>0 their cost is 0. For nonempty members the witness supremum in M008 is exactly ediam(Uᵢ)^a, and the sum, cover condition and scale constraint are identical. Thus M008 gives H^a(A)=sup_{δ>0}C_a(A,δ). If δ₁≤δ₂ then every δ₁-cover is a δ₂-cover, so C_a(A,δ₁)≥C_a(A,δ₂); consequently the decreasing-scale limit equals that supremum. M001 gives H^s(E)=∞, hence for every finite K there is δ₀>0 such that 0<δ≤δ₀ implies C_s(E,δ)>K. Fix δ>0 and any Nat-indexed δ-cover (Vᵢ) of F. Put ρᵢ=ediam(Vᵢ), Aᵢ=π₁(Vᵢ), Bᵢ=π₂(Vᵢ). Projection does not increase diameter in the concatenated Euclidean metric, hence diam(Aᵢ),diam(Bᵢ)≤ρᵢ≤δ. Choose ηᵢ=ε·2^(−(i+1))/(1+ρᵢ^s)>0. Since Bᵢ is bounded with diameter ≤ρᵢ, its infimum and supremum are finite; choose an open interval Jᵢ containing Bᵢ by extending the enclosing interval at both ends with total added length ηᵢ. Then length(Jᵢ)≤ρᵢ+ηᵢ. For every t∈[0,1] and x∈E, (x,t) lies in some Vᵢ, so x∈Aᵢ and t∈Bᵢ⊆Jᵢ. Therefore {Aᵢ:t∈Jᵢ} covers E, with diameters ≤δ, and the definition of infimum yields C_s(E,δ)≤∑'ᵢ 1_{Jᵢ∩[0,1]}(t)ρᵢ^s pointwise. Equip [0,1] with the restricted measure ν=volume.restrict([0,1]). Each Jᵢ∩[0,1] is Borel; its indicator multiplied by the constant ρᵢ^s is measurable, hence AEMeasurable for ν. The restricted mass is ν([0,1])=volume([0,1])=ofReal(1−0)=1, using M011. Integrate the pointwise inequality with ν and apply M009. Apply M002 to the countable measurable summands to interchange lintegral and tsum. By M010 each term integrates to ρᵢ^s·ν(Jᵢ∩[0,1]). The inclusion Jᵢ∩[0,1]⊆[aᵢ,bᵢ] and M013 give ν(Jᵢ∩[0,1])≤volume([aᵢ,bᵢ]); M011 evaluates the latter as ofReal(bᵢ−aᵢ)≤ofReal(ρᵢ+ηᵢ). Thus the term is at most ρᵢ^s(ρᵢ+ηᵢ). Summing, C_s(E,δ)≤∑'ᵢρᵢ^(s+1)+∑'ᵢηᵢρᵢ^s≤∑'ᵢρᵢ^(s+1)+ε, since ηᵢρᵢ^s≤ε·2^(−(i+1)) and the geometric series over i∈ℕ is at most 1. This holds for every ε>0 with the cover fixed; therefore C_s(E,δ)≤∑'ᵢρᵢ^(s+1), including infinite sums (if the sum is ⊤ the claim is immediate; otherwise use the order characterization by all positive ε). Since the cover was arbitrary, take the infimum over all Nat-indexed δ-covers of F: C_s(E,δ)≤C_(s+1)(F,δ). Taking δ↓0, the left side tends to ⊤, so C_(s+1)(F,δ) tends to ⊤; the exact M008 supremum/content identity gives H^(s+1)(F)=⊤. Apply M001's threshold theorem at the NNReal coercion of s+1 to infer s+1≤dim_H(F). As this holds for every 0<s<D, the order density of reals gives D+1≤dim_H(F) when D>0.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/0/text\",\"value\":\"Let D=dim_H(E), F=E×[0,1] with the prescribed concatenated Euclidean metric. First establish 0≤D≤n<∞. Hausdorff dimension is nonnegative. If n=0, ℝ⁰ is a singleton and E is that singleton, so D=0. If n>0, compactness H002 implies boundedness, so E is contained in a fixed bounded box. For each 0<h≤1 subdivide the box into grid cubes of side h. There is a constant C independent of h with at most C h^(−n) cubes; each has diameter at most √n h. For every m>n the sum of m-power diameters is at most C h^(−n)(√n h)^m=C n^(m/2)h^(m−n), which tends to zero as h↓0. The scale-cover definition of Hausdorff measure then gives H^m(E)=0 and hence dim_H(E)≤n. Now fix q>D. Choose its NNReal exponent d_q and real coercion. M003 gives H^q(E)=0. By the exact M008 formula, H^q(E)=sup_{r>0}C_q(E,r)=0. Since contents are nonnegative, C_q(E,r)=0 for every r>0. By the definition of infimum, for every r>0 and every γ>0 there is a Nat-indexed r-cover (Uᵢ) of E whose sum of q-costs is <γ. Indeed the admissible family is nonempty (cover by E followed by empty sets if its diameter is within r; more generally use singleton cover), and if its infimum is zero a cost below γ exists. Choose scales r_j↓0 and γ_j>0 with γ_j→0, and such covers. For each nonempty Uᵢ with positive diameter dᵢ≤r_j retain Uᵢ. For each nonempty zero-diameter member, it is a singleton in the Euclidean metric; replace it by an open ball of positive radius so small that the sum of all added q-costs is less than γ_j. This is possible by assigning the k-th such singleton a ball radius with q-power less than γ_j2^(−k−1); countably many replacements then have total extra cost <γ_j. Empty members remain empty. We now have a countable cover with all retained nonempty diameters positive and total q-cost <2γ_j. For each set of diameter dᵢ≤r_j, cover [0,1] by at most 1/dᵢ+1 closed subintervals of length at most dᵢ (partition into equal pieces). The products Uᵢ×Kᵢℓ cover E×[0,1], and their product diameters are at most √(dᵢ²+dᵢ²)=√2 dᵢ. For r_j≤1, the number of interval pieces is at most 2/dᵢ, so the total (q+1)-cost contributed by Uᵢ is at most (2/dᵢ)(√2dᵢ)^(q+1)=2(√2)^(q+1)dᵢ^q. Summing gives at most 2(√2)^(q+1)·2γ_j, which tends to zero. These are countable covers of F at scales √2r_j→0, so M008's supremum/infimum formula implies H^(q+1)(F)=0. M012 then gives dim_H(F)≤q+1. Since this holds for every q>D, density of the reals yields dim_H(F)≤D+1. In the n=0 case, F is isometric to [0,1]; alternatively cover it by intervals of lengths tending to zero to obtain the same upper bound D+1=1. The isometry preserves diameters and the M008 Hausdorff measure formula.\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and ma